Polish start window, card tables and code scrollbars

Purpose:
Visual touch-ups. Markdown tables in cards had no separation; the
desktop start window stacked three clashing blue bands with black
titles; code blocks showed the heavy default scrollbar.

Approach:
- style.css: card tables get tight cells, hairline row/column rules,
  a tinted header and faint zebra rows. Code blocks (pre) get a thin,
  trackless scrollbar. Both use translucent grays instead of theme
  variables, so every light and dark theme works unchanged.
- home.css: New/Open/Import share one header band side by side; recent
  documents become one bordered list on a neutral background. Colours
  are home-only variables on :root.

Constraints:
- CSS only; no Elm or markup changes.
- Header cells keep markdown column alignment (align attribute).
- The #document horizontal scrollbar stays as upstream styles it.

